 "description": "This web service illustrates the estimated resident population (ERP) and components of change (births, deaths, migration), by&nbsp;Statistical Area Level 2 (SA2)&nbsp;as released in Regional population. ERP is the official estimate of the Australian population, which links people to a place of usual residence within Australia (for further details, see&nbsp;Regional population methodology). The full dataset and additional information are available in the&nbsp;Regional population&nbsp;publication.\nKey Features:\n\nGeography level:&nbsp;Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3,&nbsp;Statistical Area Level 2 (SA2)\nERP for each year 30 June 2001 to 30 June 2025\nERP change number and per cent for 2024-25\nArea in km2 Population density per km2\nComponents of population change for each year 2021-22 to 2024-25 (births, deaths, natural increase, internal migration arrivals, internal migration departures, net internal migration, overseas migration arrivals, overseas migration departures, net overseas migration)\n\nKey Attributes:\n\n\n\nField alias\nField name\nDescription\n\n\nState&nbsp;Code 2021\nstate_code_2021\n2021 State/Territory codes from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nState Name 2021\nstate_name_2021\n2021 State/Territory names from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nGreater Capital City Statistical Areas 2021 code\ngccsa_code_2021\n2021 Greater Capital City Statistical Areas (GCCSA) codes from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3\n\n\nGreater Capital City Statistical Areas 2021 name\ngccsa_name_2021\n2021 Greater Capital City Statistical Areas (GCCSA) names from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level&nbsp;4 2021 code\nsa4_code_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level&nbsp;4 (SA4) codes from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level 4 2021 name\nsa4_name_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level&nbsp;4 (SA4) names from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level&nbsp;3 2021 code\nsa3_code_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level&nbsp;3 (SA3) codes from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level 3 2021 name\nsa3_name_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level&nbsp;3 (SA3) names from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3.\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level 2 2021 code\nsa2_code_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level 2 (SA2) codes from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3. SA2s are medium-sized general purpose areas built to represent communities that interact together socially and economically.\n\n\nStatistical Areas Level 2 2021 name\nsa2_name_2021\n2021 Statistical Areas Level 2 (SA2) names from the Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS), Edition 3. SA2s are medium-sized general purpose areas built to represent communities that interact together socially and economically.\n\n\nEstimated resident population 2001 to 2025\nerp_2001 to erp_2025\nEstimated resident population for 30 June 2001 to 30 June 2025.&nbsp;\n\n\nEstimated resident population change number 2024-25\nerp_change_number_2024_25\nNumerical change in the estimated resident population between 2024 and 2025.\n\n\nEstimated resident population change percentage 2024-25\nerp_change_per_cent_2024_25\nPercentage change in the estimated resident population between 2024 and 2025.\n\n\nArea in square kilometres\narea_km2\nArea of a region in square kilometres, based on the Albers equal area conic projection.\n\n\nPopulation density 2025 (people/km&sup2;)\npop_density_2025_people_per_km2\nPopulation density in 2025, measured as people per square kilometre.\n\n\nBirths 2021-22 to 2024-25\nbirths_2021_22 to births_2024_25\nNumber of registered births for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nDeaths 2021-22&nbsp;to 2024-25\ndeaths_2021_22 to deaths_2024_25\nNumber of registered deaths for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.&nbsp;\n\n\nNatural increase 2021-22 to 2024-25\nnatural_increase_2021_22 to natural_increase_2024_25\nNumber of births minus number of deaths for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nInternal arrivals 2021-22 to 2024-25\ninternal_arrivals_2021_22 to internal_arrivals_2024_25\nNumber of arrivals into the area from any other area in Australia for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nInternal departures&nbsp; 2021-22 to 2024-25\ninternal_departures_2021_22 to internal_departures_2024_25\nNumber of departures out of the area to any other area in Australia for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nNet internal migration 2021-22 to 2024-25\nnet_internal_migration_2021_22 to net_internal_migration_2024_25\nNumber of internal arrivals minus number of internal departures for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.&nbsp;\n\n\nOverseas arrivals 2021-22 to 2024-25\noverseas_arrivals_2021_22 to overseas_arrivals_2024_25\nNumber of arrivals into the area from overseas for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nOverseas departures 2021-22 to 2024-25\noverseas_departures_2021_22 to overseas_departures_2024_25\nNumber of departures out of the area to overseas for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\nNet overseas migration 2021-22 to 2024-25\nnet_overseas_migration_2021_22 to net_overseas_migration_2024_25\nNumber of overseas arrivals minus number of overseas departures for 2021&ndash;22 to 2024&ndash;25.\n\n\n\nData and geography references\n\nMain source data publication: Regional population\nGeographic boundary information: Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3\nFurther information: Regional population methodology\nSource: Australian Bureau of Statistics (ABS)\n\nContact the Australian Bureau of Statistics\n\nEmail geography@abs.gov.au if you have any questions or feedback about this web service.\nSubscribe to get updates on ABS web services and geospatial products.\n\nPrivacy at the Australian Bureau of Statistics\n\nRead how the ABS manages personal information: ABS privacy policy.\n",
